worker_module_budget
  module "formal_ai_worker_program_ir.js"
  ceiling 425
  rationale "Issue #1138 pure browser coding IR, bounded typed fragment search, source attribution, and honest unverified lowering parity with native composition. Since the meanings seed split (issue #960 R222-1) the browser fragment catalog bootstraps meanings-coding-structure-2.lino as a second seed part, mirroring rust/src/coding/fragment_catalog.rs bootstrap_from (+4). IrType::OrderedSequence unification parity with the native rules (ordered unifies into sequence, never the reverse) added +14. Wiring the closed-program selection module into the complete-candidate filter, carrying application counts for least-action selection, and the binder-mention slot preference added +13. The ceiling moved 338 to 369 to record that parity work; candidate-selection logic itself lives in formal_ai_worker_closed_programs.js. PR #1188 dogfooding (+3): the unused-parameter rank counts whole identifiers, as native collect_parameter_names does, so `a` is no longer read by `math`. PR #1188 dogfooding (+27): binder preference only for slots the idiom binds (browserBinderSlots, native fragment_binder_slots), parameter reads ahead of slot-name coherence in the pool and slot choices, and parameters always offered as slot operands, so `add3(a, b, c)` composes `a + b + c`. PR #1188 T1 (+26): fragments carry their seeded `realization` blocks and compose in the named language when the seed lowers functions into it (browserFunctionTemplate reads `{language}_ir_function` from coding-discovery-runtime.lino, as native ir_lowering does; browserSynthesisLanguage), so `export function multiply(a, b)` is lowered from the same IR as the Python `def`."
